          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Which chapter holds high blood pressure, and what does that chapter deliberately exclude?",
          "answer": "High blood pressure is covered in the ICD-10-CM Chapter 9, which focuses on diseases of the circulatory system (codes I00-I99). However, there are certain exclusions regarding its classification.\n\nKey exclusions include:\n\n1. **Pregnancy-related Hypertension:** Any hypertension that complicates pregnancy, childbirth, or the postpartum period is excluded from this chapter and is instead classified in the obstetric chapter using specific pregnancy codes.\n\n2. **Isolated Readings:** A single elevated reading or a series of readings in someone who has not been diagnosed with hypertension is considered an abnormal finding rather than a disease. Such findings are classified in Chapter 18, which deals with symptoms and abnormal findings.\n\nThese exclusions highlight that documentation and the context of hypertension are crucial in determining its classification (source: \"ICD-10-CM Chapter 9: diseases of the circulatory system\").\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
